# --- Research sub-modules ------------------------------------------------------
# The sub-module directories are tracked as gitlinks (mode 160000), and
# .gitignore has NO effect on them: a tracked path is never ignored. Patterns
# such as "napari/" here used to be dead weight.
#
# What actually keeps `git status` clean is `ignore = dirty` in .gitmodules:
#
#     [submodule "napari"]
#         ignore = dirty
#
# Without it, untracked files inside a sub-module are reported as
# "modified: napari (untracked content)". Inspect a sub-module with:
#
#     git -C <submodule> status
#
# Do NOT add unanchored patterns for directories that also occur inside the
# evidence packs: a bare "napari/" would also match
# "PYQT6-GENESIS-PACKAGING/external-PyQt6-Apps/napari-results/_evidence/src/napari/", the four
# napari source files pinned there as evidence.

# --- Python / TBO -------------------------------------------------------------
# General Python build artefacts (in case packaging happens in-tree).
# Root-anchored so they cannot swallow a nested directory of the same name
# inside an evidence pack.
/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
/build/
/dist/
/.venv/
/venv/
.coverage
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/

# --- The two owner applications ------------------------------------------------
# TBO and Lucio IVA Calculator are the owner's own applications, and they are
# pinned as sub-modules like the other six studied trees:
#
#     my-PyQt6-Apps/TBO/
#     my-PyQt6-Apps/lucio-iva-calculator/
#
# There is deliberately NO ignore rule for them, and adding one would be
# useless: a sub-module is tracked as a gitlink (mode 160000), and a tracked
# path is never ignored. What keeps `git status` quiet when those trees have
# build output or a venv inside them is `ignore = dirty` in .gitmodules, which
# all eight sub-modules now carry.
#
# Their studies and evidence packs live next to them, at
# `my-PyQt6-Apps/<app>-resultados/`, and THOSE are tracked. That is the reason
# this file has to stay anchored: while they were independent clones a bare
# `PyQt6-Apps/` pattern was added here, and it silently swallowed everything
# under the directory — including the two `*-resultados/` folders that must be
# committed. See AGENTS.md section 5.
